  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = x^{2} + bx + 7\\), where \\(b\\) is a constant. If \\(f(2) = 3\\), what is the value of \\(b\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-4"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "\\(f(2) = 2^{2} + 2b + 7 = 11 + 2b\\).",
    "\\(11 + 2b = 3\\), so \\(2b = -8\\) and \\(b = -4\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
